DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-25-sl23-number", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 656--656", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "\\begin{equation}\\hypertarget{tag-024M}{}\\label{maps:eq:D.SL23}", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (proof guard):lines 20656--20656", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "\\tag{D.SL23}\\hypertarget{tag-024M}{}\\label{maps:eq:D.SL23}", "reason": "Replace the inherited manual SL number by automatic section equation numbering; preserve the exact permanent label and hypertarget. The separate D25/D20 rows give the hatted orientation transport for SL15, SL16 and SL20.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D19"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-26-sl24-number", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 571--571", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "\\begin{equation}\\hypertarget{tag-024N}{}\\label{maps:eq:D.SL24}", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (proof guard):lines 20628--20628", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "\\tag{D.SL24}\\hypertarget{tag-024N}{}\\label{maps:eq:D.SL24}", "reason": "Replace the inherited manual SL number by automatic section equation numbering; preserve the exact permanent label and hypertarget. The separate D25/D20 rows give the hatted orientation transport for SL15, SL16 and SL20.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D19"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-27-basis-certificate-wording", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 15--19", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "There are twelve marked star positions of this type\nin the natural catalogue: the eight primitive-gamma $I_1^*$\npositions of \\ref{maps:src:D.2.27} and the four primitive-gamma $I_3^*$\npositions. Their unimodular bases are given in the proof.\nThe conclusions hold for every marked boundary with the displayed basis.", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (statement guard):lines 20178--20183", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "There are twelve actual marked star positions of this type\nin the natural catalogue: the eight primitive-gamma $I_1^*$\npositions of \\ref{maps:src:D.2.27} and the four primitive-gamma $I_3^*$\npositions. Their unimodular bases are retained in the\ncertificate below. The theorem also applies to any further\ninput for which the displayed integral marked basis is supplied.", "reason": "Give the twelve basis formulas and their inverses in the mathematical proof; replace file/certificate workflow terminology without changing the displayed-basis scope.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D08"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-28-peripheral-lift-wording", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 26--26", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "part of the peripheral marking.", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (statement guard):lines 20190--20190", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "retained in the peripheral marking.", "reason": "State that the integer lift is part of the mathematical marking.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D08"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-29-root-unit-wording", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 32--34", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "Every $j,r$ and every such $N$ is realized by a free\naffine root action. Its maps include the holomorphic unit factors\nand integer affine twists.", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (statement guard):lines 20196--20198", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "Every $j,r$ and every such $N$ is realized by an actual free\naffine root action. All its holomorphic unit factors and\ninteger affine twists are retained.", "reason": "Describe the free root maps, units and integer twists as mathematical data.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D08"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-30-normal-origin-marking", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 62--63", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "Let $D,L$ be the fixed normal tori defined by the marked origin\nsection in the $\\delta,\\ell$ directions.", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (statement guard):lines 20226--20227", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "Let $D,L$ be its literal fixed-normal tori in the\n$\\delta,\\ell$ directions.", "reason": "Specify the origin-section convention used by the full Wang section and its inverse; the geometric tori are unchanged.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D20"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-31-positive-kernel-wording", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 73--76", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "These equations specify integral sublattices with projected indices\n$k,k/2,2k$ in the full fixed lattice. The boundary cokernel is free\nof rank $\\rho-1$. The last row includes the cap summand\n$\\mathbb Z/2$ and the nonzero torsion coordinates of both fibre images.", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (statement guard):lines 20237--20243", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "These are unsaturated marked kernels where appropriate.\nTheir projected indices in the full fixed lattice are\nrespectively $k,k/2,2k$. The boundary cokernel is free of\nrank $\\rho-1$. In particular the last row retains the\nactual cap $\\mathbb Z/2$ and its nonzero fibre correction;\nit is not a conclusion from rational ranks or determinant\norders alone.", "reason": "State the exact integral sublattices, indices, full free cokernel and both nonzero torsion coordinates positively; remove the defensive rank/determinant comparison.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D02"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-32-bar-presentation-wording", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 78--85", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "These columns enter the integral\nbar presentation of \\ref{maps:src:D.2.41} or \\ref{maps:src:D.2.46}. A vector $(0,b,c,d)$\ncontributes the regular-fibre representative of\n$bw$, together with $c$ times the marked $\\delta$ sweep\nand $d$ times the marked $\\ell$ sweep. The cap contributes\n$\\rho$ to the free relative rank in \\eqref{maps:eq:D.GI10} and zero to\nthe Euler number. The same presentation includes the other cap\nchoices and their full finite Thom columns.", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (statement guard):lines 20245--20252", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "These columns can be inserted directly into the integral\nbar algorithm of \\ref{maps:src:D.2.41} or \\ref{maps:src:D.2.46}. A vector $(0,b,c,d)$\ncontributes the actual regular-fibre representative of\n$bw$, together with $c$ times the marked $\\delta$ sweep\nand $d$ times the marked $\\ell$ sweep. The cap contributes\n$\\rho$ to the free relative rank in \\eqref{maps:eq:D.GI10} and zero to\nthe Euler number. Thus all other already proved cap\nchoices and full finite Thom columns can be retained.", "reason": "Use the integral bar presentation and marked representatives; retain every other cap/finite Thom column at its proved scope.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D08"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-33-homology-scope-disclaimer", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 115--123", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "Cyclic summands of order one are omitted. For example,\nthe six default natural rows with $b_0=4$ admit the\nsimply connected choice $s=\\pm1$, $k=2h$, $j$ even.\nIt has\n\\begin{equation}\\hypertarget{tag-024U}{}\\label{maps:eq:D.SL9}\nH_2=H_4=\\mathbb Z^{nh},\\qquad\n                         H_3=\\mathbb Z^{2nh}.\n\\end{equation}\nHere $n=1$ on OS50/default and $n=3$ on OS46/default.", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (statement guard):lines 20291--20292", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "These are nonminimal star-log outputs, and no smooth\nclassification is inferred from their homology.", "reason": "The statement gives homology and a fundamental-group specialization. Remove the repeated disclaimer without adding any smooth-classification conclusion.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D11"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-34-affine-heading", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 172--172", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "\\emph{Flat sections and the holomorphic root.}", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (proof guard):lines 20299--20299", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "\\emph{The actual unbounded affine actions.}", "reason": "Use the mathematical subject of the complete period/root construction as the proof heading.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D08"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-35-missing-parity-heading", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 434--434", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "\\emph{The fibre and the complete torsion marking.}", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (proof guard):lines 20461--20461", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "\\emph{The regular-fibre map and its missing parity.}", "reason": "Remove wording about a missing earlier parity calculation; prove the complete marked torsion map.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D01"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-36-unit-collar-reason", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 278--301", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "The period units give the same marked smooth diagrams by explicit\nmaps. Interpolate their logarithms while fixing integer winding,\nand interpolate $\\tau$ in the upper half-plane, keeping the\nanti-invariance of $\\eta,\\epsilon$. In a node equation $XY=sV$,\ndivide $Y$ by $V$; multiplication is the inverse. In line frames\nuse the exponential of the chosen logarithm and its reciprocal.\nAt a pole translation subtract its real lift multiplied\nby a collar function equal to zero and one at the two ends;\naddition is the inverse. The derivatives of these chart maps\ngive lifts of the interval direction tangent to all central strata.\nAn invariant partition of unity and finite averaging give one\nsuch lift on the compact proper tube. Its flow and reverse flow\nare inverse maps, preserving the prescribed outer marking.\n\nThe cap retracts onto this central gluing. For an invariant\nHermitian metric put $f_0=|s|^2$. On $XY=s$ one has\n$\\|\\nabla f_0\\|\\ge c f_0^{3/4}$, with one positive $c$\nafter metric comparison on the finite atlas. The normalized\nnegative-gradient flow has tail length at most\n$4c^{-1}f_0^{1/4}$, so its limiting collapse is continuous and\nfixes the central fibre. A compact proper tube prevents escape\nthrough a side boundary. Reverse flow gives the inverse on\npositive-radius annular collars. The invariant construction\ndescends under the free action.", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (proof guard):lines 20341--20345", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "The usual root-and-unit isotopy keeps these\nintegral characters and all component meridians.\nThus the following topological calculation\napplies to each actual action, not merely to\nan abstract permutation of components.", "reason": "Supply the explicit logarithmic unit maps, inverse collars, invariant flow, proper tube and normalized-gradient retraction needed by the original short isotopy assertion.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D22"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-37-independent-wang-placement", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 384--406", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "Consequently \\eqref{maps:eq:D.SL12} is the entire $H_2$\npresentation, with no omitted degree-one bridge.\n\nWhen $f=1$, all paired sections are $2D_0$ and\n$\\widehat F_{\\rm fixed}=2\\widehat\\sigma_{\\rm fixed}-2D_0$.\nWhen $f=2$, each fixed end satisfies\n$\\widehat F_i=2\\widehat\\sigma_i-S$.\nThese substitutions, reversed for the inverse, give free rank\n$\\rho+1$. When $f=0$ all sections equal $2D_0$ and\n\\begin{equation}\\hypertarget{tag-024B}{}\\label{maps:eq:D.SL13}\nS=2D_0=2D_1,\\qquad \\tau_2=D_1-D_0,\\qquad 2\\tau_2=0 .\n\\end{equation}\nFor section coefficients $c_i$ and endpoint coefficients\n$d_0,d_1$, the exact residual quotient is\n$(d_0+d_1+2\\sum c_i,[d_1]_2)$.\nIts inverse includes $D_0$ and $D_1-D_0$.\nThus $\\tau_2$ has exact order two.\nThe injective $H_2$ conductor map leaves\n$H_3(U)=\\mathbb Z^{2\\rho}$ and $H_4(U)=\\mathbb Z^\\rho$.\nThe $H_3$ generators are the sphere fibres over the two base\ncircles on each normalization, with inverse integration over\nthe sphere fibre; the $H_4$ generators are its fundamental\nclasses. All higher groups vanish.", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (proof guard):lines 20449--20459", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "As an\nindependent calculation, choose a primitive\nquotient gamma circle. The cap is a mapping\ntorus of $I_q\\times S^1_\\lambda$; on its\ncomponent spheres the return is the\nreflection, while on the actual specialized\ntorus $t=[\\beta\\lambda]$ naturality of the\nexterior-square action gives\n$t\\mapsto-t-\\sum_iF_i$. Its integral Wang\nsequence gives the same groups, including\nthe order-two summand in \\eqref{maps:eq:D.SL13}.", "reason": "Retain one normalization proof in the receiver. The entire independent Wang calculation, cut/sheet inverse and coordinate transport are proved in post-exposure note section 2 and compared in item 7.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D12"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-38-complex-orientation-sign", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 451--458", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "In the displayed holomorphic chart, $\\alpha$ is the positive\nangular coordinate and $\\beta$ moves radially outward.\nThus the ordered $\\alpha\\beta$ torus specializes to minus the\nsum of the complex-oriented ruling spheres. In the hatted\ncoordinates this gives exactly\n\\begin{equation}\\hypertarget{tag-024D}{}\\label{maps:eq:D.SL15}\n2x=-\\sum_v|v|\\widehat F_v,\\qquad 2w=-kS .\n\\end{equation}", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (proof guard):lines 20465--20467", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "The regular torus $\\alpha\\beta$\nspecializes to the sum of the $q$ complex\ncomponent spheres, each with degree one.", "reason": "The ordered angular/outward-radial torus has negative complex orientation for beta=-q log(s)/(2pi i)+unit. Correct this intermediate assertion only. The explicit hatted conductor involution and inverse preserve all theorem conclusions and the numerical SL15/SL16/SL20 formulas; refined receiver id maps:src:D.2.49.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D25"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-39-ruling-coordinate-convention", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 351--367", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "We distinguish the geometric complex-oriented classes from the\nfollowing transported homology coordinates:\n\\[\n\\widehat F_v=-F_v,\\qquad\n\\widehat\\sigma_v=\n\\begin{cases}S-\\sigma_v,&v\\text{ fixed},\\\\\n\\sigma_v,&v\\text{ paired},\\end{cases}\n\\]\nwhere $S$ is the common conductor section class.\nFix $S$ and all $D_e$ under this change. It is an involution.\nA fixed-vertex relation changes to its negative plus\n$2(S-d_eD_e)$, an integral sum of the conductor relations\nalong the interval; paired-vertex relations are fixed.\nThus this is an exact integral change of presentation with\nthe same inverse. Hatted vectors are homology coordinates;\nthe complex orientation and section-square assertion above\nrefer to the unhatted geometric classes.", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (proof guard):lines 20377--20382", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "Choose a section $\\sigma$ with\n$\\sigma^2=1$ and denote its complex sphere\nfibre by $F$. Its connected conductor\nbisection has class $2\\sigma-F$; its\nself-intersection is zero because the pole\nnormal line becomes trivial on the cover.", "reason": "Keep the complex geometric F and section square separate from Fhat=-F and fixed sigmahat=S-sigma. The involution fixes every double curve, carries each relation by its stated integral chain map, and is its own inverse.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D20"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-40-nonabelian-group-notation", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 409--417", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "\\begin{equation}\\hypertarget{tag-024C}{}\\label{maps:eq:D.SL14}\n\\begin{split}\n\\Gamma=\\langle\\beta,\\lambda,\\ell,g\\mid&\n[\\beta,\\lambda]=[\\beta,\\ell]=[\\lambda,\\ell]=1,\\\\\n&g\\beta g^{-1}=\\beta^{-1}\\lambda^{-n},\\\n[g,\\lambda]=[g,\\ell]=1,\\\ng^{2k}=\\lambda^R\\ell^N\\rangle .\n\\end{split}\n\\end{equation}", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (proof guard):lines 20434--20441", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "\\begin{gathered}\n \\Gamma=\\langle\\beta,\\lambda,\\ell,g\\mid\n [\\beta,\\lambda]=[\\beta,\\ell]=[\\lambda,\\ell]=1,\\\\\n g\\beta g^{-1}=-\\beta-n\\lambda,\\quad\n [g,\\lambda]=[g,\\ell]=1,\\quad\n                    2kg=R\\lambda+N\\ell\\rangle .\n\\end{gathered}                                             \\tag{D.SL14}\\hypertarget{tag-024C}{}\\label{maps:eq:D.SL14}\n\\]", "reason": "Write the cap relation multiplicatively before abelianization, with its exact lift/inverse words; preserve the same group and permanent identity.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D20"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-41-torsion-cokernel-wording", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 536--540", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "Killing the two fibre images sets $\\tau_2=kD_0$ and\n$2kD_0=0$, so the finite part of the fibre cokernel is\ncyclic $\\mathbb Z/(2k)$, with these exact inverse coordinates.\nFor $f=1,2$ its corresponding finite part is $\\mathbb Z/k$\nand $\\mathbb Z/(k/2)$.", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (proof guard):lines 20559--20564", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "Both order-two terms are forced by the\nactual classifying map. In particular the\nfibre cokernel has cyclic torsion\n$\\mathbb Z/(2k)$ in this case; replacing\nthe second image by $-kD_0$ would give a\ndifferent marked map.", "reason": "Give the cyclic quotient and inverse tau-to-kD0 coordinate directly, instead of contrasting it with an omitted torsion term.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D02"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-42-normal-lift-convention", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 574--583", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "Its inverse adds $hnw$, since\n$[\\delta\\beta]=0$ and $[\\beta\\ell]=nw$.\nAt $f=0$ the new chosen-centre class is\n$D_0=D_{0,\\rm old}+h\\tau_2$.\nThus \\eqref{maps:eq:D.SL22}, in the old conductor marking,\nhas $L=-RD_{0,\\rm old}+h\\tau_2$.\nThe free relation already forces the coefficient of $L$\nto be even, so its contribution to a kernel relation is zero.\nThese formulas give the correction for every positive or\nnegative integer lift.", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (proof guard):lines 20630--20643", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "Here the first symbol denotes the old normal\ntorus, not a double-curve class. Indeed\n$[\\delta\\beta]=0$ and $[\\beta\\ell]=nw$\nin \\eqref{maps:eq:D.SL4}. Substituting \\eqref{maps:eq:D.SL24} into\nthe kernel formulas replaces $R_0$ by\n$R$ exactly. In the $f=0$ case it changes\nthe displayed image of $L$ in \\eqref{maps:eq:D.SL22} to\n$-RD_0+h\\tau$, but the equation in\n\\eqref{maps:eq:D.SL5} already forces its coefficient\n$d$ to be even; the kernel parity is\ntherefore still precisely $b$ even.\nThus integer affine lifts are included\nwithout suppressing their actual torsion\ncorrection.", "reason": "Distinguish the old normal torus from the old endpoint class. Show D0=D0old+h tau, the old-frame L correction and both inverse substitutions for every integer lift.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D20"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-43-primitive-cokernel-lifts", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 613--626", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "The full boundary image has primitive complement\n$\\mathbb Z^{\\rho-1}$. Here are explicit lifts for its\nremaining conductor coordinates.\nFor $f=1$ choose $pk+t(2N)=1$ and use $-pw+tD$ for $D_0$.\nFor $f=2$ choose $p(k/2)+tN=1$ and use the same expression\nfor $S$. For $f=0$ choose $pk+tN=1$ and put\n$V=-2pw+tD$. Then\n$D_0=-L+(1-R)V/2$ and $\\tau_2=w+kD_0$.\nBoth expressions are integral and have the asserted free\nand torsion coordinates. Together with the primitive $x$\ncoordinate and the normalization substitutions, these are\ninverse quotient maps proving the entire free cokernel.\nEquivalently it injects into\n$H_2(U,\\partial U)=H^4(U)=\\mathbb Z^\\rho$.", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (proof guard):lines 20609--20613", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "The cokernel of the full boundary map is\nfree of rank $\\rho-1$, as one sees directly\nfrom \\eqref{maps:eq:D.SL12} and \\eqref{maps:eq:D.SL16}--\\eqref{maps:eq:D.SL22}.\nEquivalently, Poincare--Lefschetz duality\nputs it into the free group $H^4(U)$.", "reason": "Supply explicit Bezout lifts of the conductor and torsion generators and the inverse quotient maps; the duality injection gives the same free cokernel.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D22"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-44-duality-typography", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 625--626", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "Equivalently it injects into\n$H_2(U,\\partial U)=H^4(U)=\\mathbb Z^\\rho$.", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (proof guard):lines 20612--20612", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "Poincare--Lefschetz", "reason": "Replace the unaccented duality-name shorthand by the exact integral duality isomorphism used.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D23"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-45-global-inverse-quotients", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 659--677", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "Set $u=b-4ec$ and $s=N-2ke$.\nFor $f=1$ the condition is $ku+Rd=2sc$.\nChoose $v k=1\\bmod 2|s|$. The relation lattice has basis\n$(2Bs,0),(-BvR,1)$.\nIts quotient map is\n$(x,y)\\mapsto[x+BvRy]_{2B|s|}$, with inverse $[z]\\mapsto zs_0$.\nFor $f=2$, choose $v(k/2)=1\\bmod |s|$ and replace\n$2s,R$ by $s,R/2$ in those maps. This gives\n$\\mathbb Z/(B|s|)$, also when $|s|=1$.\nFor $f=0$ both $u,d$ are even. Write $u=2u_0,d=2d_0$,\nchoose $vk=1\\bmod |s|$, and obtain the columns\n$(2Bs,0),(-2BvR,2)$.\nWith $Y_0=L-BvR s_0$ the inverse quotient maps are\n\\[\n(x,y)\\longmapsto\n([x+BvRy]_{2B|s|},[y]_2),\\qquad\n([z],[t])\\longmapsto zs_0+tY_0 .\n\\]\nThese prove the full torsion groups at all parameters.", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (proof guard):lines 20658--20675", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "Set $u=b-4ec$ and $s=N-2ke$.\nFor $f=1$ its defining condition becomes\n$ku+Rd=2sc$. Since $k$ is odd and prime\nto $2s$, $d$ is unrestricted and\n$u$ is a fixed residue modulo $2s$.\nThe Smith cokernel is cyclic of order\n$2B|s|$.\nFor $f=2$, the condition is\n$(k/2)u+(R/2)d=sc$.\nHere $k/2$ is prime to $s$, so the same\nargument gives a cyclic cokernel of\norder $B|s|$.\nFor $f=0$, $u$ and $d$ are even; write\n$u=2u_0,d=2d_0$. The condition becomes\n$ku_0+Rd_0=sc$. Its relation matrix has\nSmith factors $2$ and $2B|s|$.\nThis proves the three torsion groups\nin \\eqref{maps:eq:D.SL7} for every parameter.", "reason": "Give each unbounded two-generator relation basis, explicit residue quotient and inverse representative, including |s|=1 and f=0 two-torsion.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D22"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-46-seifert-vanishing-words", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 679--692", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "For the fundamental group the selected cusp and its transported\nvanishing words kill the two elliptic generators and $\\delta$.\nAt the exceptional $46/II$ position the first vanishing words\nhave index three; the star disc bounding\n$\\alpha=2e_1+\\delta$ supplies the coprime twofold relation\nand kills $e_1$, then $e_2$. The remaining fibre loop is\nthe gamma return, whose exponent gives the inverse\nquotient map. The star group is generated by its boundary,\nso van Kampen gives\n$\\langle\\gamma,c\\mid[\\gamma,c]=1,\\\nc^{2k}=\\gamma^N,\\ c=\\gamma^e\\rangle$.\nSending $\\gamma$ to $1\\bmod |s|$ and $c$ to $e$,\nwith inverse the gamma loop, proves the group claim.\n$s$ is odd, nonzero and prime to $2k$.", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (proof guard):lines 20677--20678", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "The one-log Seifert presentation gives\n$\\pi_1=\\mathbb Z/|s|$.", "reason": "Derive the actual vanishing-word quotient and gamma inverse, including the OS46/II index-three lattice and its coprime star-disc relation.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D22"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-47-integral-mv-bridge", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 694--702", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "Every boundary $H_1$ in these twelve natural diagrams is free:\nthe return matrices have only unit nonzero degree-one\nSmith factors. With $t$ boundary components the exterior\nhas $H_1$ rank $t$, and each boundary rank exceeds its\nminimal cap rank by one. The full degree-one Mayer--Vietoris\nsource and target therefore have equal rank. Its cokernel\nis the finite group just computed, so its integer kernel\nis zero. Thus $H_2$ is exactly the free component complement\n$\\mathbb Z^{\\rho-1}$ plus the displayed torsion group.", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (proof guard):lines 20680--20684", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "The free local\nboundary defect is $\\rho-1$ and there\nis no additional rational degree-one\nbridge. All other caps in the stated\ncorollary have their minimal ranks.", "reason": "Use torsion-free boundary H1, equal source/target ranks and finite cokernel to prove the entire integral degree-one MV kernel vanishes.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D22"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-48-following-program-scope", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 659--677", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "Set $u=b-4ec$ and $s=N-2ke$.\nFor $f=1$ the condition is $ku+Rd=2sc$.\nChoose $v k=1\\bmod 2|s|$. The relation lattice has basis\n$(2Bs,0),(-BvR,1)$.\nIts quotient map is\n$(x,y)\\mapsto[x+BvRy]_{2B|s|}$, with inverse $[z]\\mapsto zs_0$.\nFor $f=2$, choose $v(k/2)=1\\bmod |s|$ and replace\n$2s,R$ by $s,R/2$ in those maps. This gives\n$\\mathbb Z/(B|s|)$, also when $|s|=1$.\nFor $f=0$ both $u,d$ are even. Write $u=2u_0,d=2d_0$,\nchoose $vk=1\\bmod |s|$, and obtain the columns\n$(2Bs,0),(-2BvR,2)$.\nWith $Y_0=L-BvR s_0$ the inverse quotient maps are\n\\[\n(x,y)\\longmapsto\n([x+BvRy]_{2B|s|},[y]_2),\\qquad\n([z],[t])\\longmapsto zs_0+tY_0 .\n\\]\nThese prove the full torsion groups at all parameters.", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (following_auxiliary guard):lines 20694--20706", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "The exact script \\path{code/III/manifolds_star_log_caps.py}\nretains the twelve actual canonical bases,\nthe full normalization matrices, the\nliteral fibre and normal maps, and their\ncomplete integral kernels. It checks\nthe conductor calculation independently\nagainst the mapping-torus sequence and\ncompares the global Smith formula on\nunbounded symbolic lattices and a finite\nset of exact instances. The proof above,\nincluding the order-two marking, is\nindependent of the finite parameter\nbounds used in those corroborating runs.", "reason": "Move the program apparatus to the check comparison. Actual pinned replay is byte-identical, but source scope is 95 finite local, 1638 finite global and one local symbolic expansion; no generic symbolic global Smith or separate executed bar proof is claimed. The receiver supplies the full unbounded quotient/inverse proof.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D09"}
DEFECT {"change_id": "III-c7-02LQ-49-following-repeated-scope", "new_location": "agents/continuation7_iii_star_logs_receiving/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III_02LQ_receiving.tex:lines 5--14", "new_page": "pending final III PDF build and page review", "new_text": "Let a marked zero-free star boundary have the integral basis\n$(\\alpha,\\beta,\\lambda,\\ell)$ and monodromy\n\\begin{equation}\\hypertarget{tag-0247}{}\\label{maps:eq:D.SL1}\n\\begin{gathered}\n A\\alpha=-\\alpha,\\quad A\\beta=-\\beta-n\\lambda,\\quad\n A\\lambda=\\lambda-\\alpha,\\quad A\\ell=\\ell,\\\\\n \\delta=-\\alpha+2\\lambda,\\qquad\\gamma^*(\\ell)=1,\n \\qquad n\\in\\{1,3\\}.\n\\end{gathered}\n\\end{equation}", "old_location": "S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_III.tex (following_auxiliary guard):lines 20707--20710", "old_page": "not asserted; exact released source interval", "old_text": "Root actions with nonprimitive gamma\npower, other integral star blocks and\npositive-weight star degenerations are\noutside this theorem's stated scope.", "reason": "State the integral star-block scope in the theorem, with primitive N and the unweighted construction following there; delete the repeated following exclusion paragraph.", "review_status": "local whole comparison complete; root admission and final page review pending", "statement_id": "maps:src:D.2.49", "type": "D11"}
